  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A combo device -- boot keyboard on one interface, boot mouse on the
 next, the wireless-dongle shape -- under the per-interface walk. The
 whole-device classifier this replaces handed the entire device to the
 keyboard driver and the mouse half was unreachable, which is why no
 pointer had ever moved over USB in any bed.

 `-hid-combo` gives codex-vm's root HID device both interfaces;
 `-hid-keys` routes the scripted keys through USB alone; the `-mouse`
 timeline moves the pointer to (60,40) and presses the left button.
 `same-dev=1` proves both handles sit on ONE slot, `got=30` that the
 keyboard half still types with SET_CONFIGURATION sent exactly once,
 and `pos=60,40 btn=1` that boot mouse reports travel their own
 interrupt pipe into the folded position.

Section: Test

 The wait is bounded by the RTC rather than by an iteration count: each
 pump costs several VM exits, so a count large enough to cover the
 timeline in iterations is minutes of wall clock.

  uhc-wait-key : UsbKbd, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  uhc-wait-key (k) (want) (prev) (secs) = act
    sc <- kbd-take k
    now <- rtc-seconds 0
    if sc == want then sc
    else if secs <= 0 then 0
    else if now < 0 then uhc-wait-key k want prev secs
    else if now == prev then uhc-wait-key k want prev secs
    else uhc-wait-key k want now (secs - 1)
  end

  uhc-wait-pos : UsbMouse, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  uhc-wait-pos (m) (x) (y) (prev) (secs) = act
    let p = mouse-pump m 1024 768
    in act
      now <- rtc-seconds 0
      if if mouse-x m == x then mouse-y m == y else False then 1
      else if secs <= 0 then 0
      else if now < 0 then uhc-wait-pos m x y prev secs
      else if now == prev then uhc-wait-pos m x y prev secs
      else uhc-wait-pos m x y now (secs - 1)
    end
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    att <- usb-attach
    let k = att.ua-kbd
    in let m = att.ua-mouse
    in act
      print-line-uni ("kbd: ok=" & (if k.uk-ok then "1" else "0") & " mouse: ok=" & (if m.um-ok then "1" else "0") & " same-dev=" & (if (k.uk-dev).ud-slot == (m.um-dev).ud-slot then "1" else "0"))
      s0 <- rtc-seconds 0
      got <- uhc-wait-key k 30 s0 8
      print-line-uni ("got=" & show got)
      s1 <- rtc-seconds 0
      hit <- uhc-wait-pos m 60 40 s1 8
      print-line-uni ("pos=" & show (mouse-x m) & "," & show (mouse-y m) & " btn=" & show (mouse-buttons m) & " hit=" & show hit)
    end
  end
